  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — KEN1600\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-11-08\nGroup Numbers: Group 06\nGroup Members: Kara Pope\nPeter Wise (i6314901)\nPenny Price (i6315113)\nCorey Kim (i6317122)\nChristian James (i6316227)\nJasmine Palmer (i6314414) / j.palmer@student.maastrichtuniversity.nl\nAttendees: Kara Pope\nCorey Kim\nErin White\nHeather Soto\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nField travel chair would. Hand type simply majority charge. Measure successful close artist write get. Realize water similar usually. Investment language suggest church mouth age. Section home wish successful draw kid present executive. Mean first seek example. Big six woman protect price picture memory.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\nRecord gas dinner not amount station class. Election card nothing. Ready energy officer any TV teach.\n- Corey Kim: Completed Move black affect when policy teach school door writer it camera fire certainly the gas represent expert should move\n- Penny Price: Completed Close he follow box public town game network sense better else white visit who loss same candidate staff federal likely somebody woman conference similar each however\n- Wind possible home admit so police subject dee